# Plan Routing (opt-in only)

Do **not** proactively ask the user whether to plan, and do not bring up
planning on your own initiative — not even for heavy/multi-file tasks. Stay
silent about this and just work normally.

Only act when the **user's own words** ask for a plan first — e.g. "plan
this", "make a plan before doing it", "برنامه بریز", "پلن کن", "let's design
this first", or they explicitly name the skill.

- User did not ask for a plan → proceed with the normal agent workflow.
  Never mention this rule or offer a plan unprompted.
- User explicitly asked for a plan → read and follow
  `~/.cursor/skills/heavy-task-plan/SKILL.md` before writing any code.

If unsure whether the user is asking for a plan (ambiguous wording), it's
fine to ask a direct clarifying question — but only after they've already
signaled they want one, never as an unprompted offer.
